  "slug": "visualization-gfaidx-7f7d",
  "summary": "New RNA scoring metrics, nucleic acid structure alignment and a critique of AF3 ion handling refine how predicted biomolecular structures are judged and searched.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is evaluating and comparing biomolecular structures and annotations rather than generating new predictors. The perspective on AlphaFold-style methods reports persistent limitations and shows that explicit potassium ions shift AF3 predictions. GSP supplies a multi-scale normalized score for 3D RNA and RNP complex predictions, while GTalign is extended to RNA/DNA structure search and alignment with higher TM-score accuracy than benchmarked tools. RNAhub2 adds prefiltering and compression to scale structure-based RNA homology searches. Related sequence-level comparison appears in TREAD, a supervised repeat annotator using protein language model embeddings that outperforms HMMER. New here are nucleic-acid-specific metrics and alignment, plus explicit consideration of ions in judging model quality.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
